port*&#x2A;: Full right-to-left layout support for international audiences &#x2A;(in development)*"],[1715,"**Scales**: VisX's `scaleBand` and `scaleLinear` for efficient coordinate mapping"],[1712,"**Screen reader support**: Semantic HTML structure with proper ARIA attributes"],[1203,"**SegmentedController Container:** `data-disabled`"],[1204,"**SegmentedControllerItem:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1266,"**Shared structural containers.** These generic, layout-only components are the building blocks for composing a component's interior (a `Modal`, a card, a panel). They are semantic containers built on `Flex`, so they accept the same layout props (`direction`, `gap`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent`, `padding`, ...)."],[279,"**Shift + Tab**: Moves focus to the previous checkbox"],[1746,"**Simplify tooltips**: If tooltips are complex, consider using simpler content or disabling them"],[1683,"**Single and multi-series support**: Display one or multiple data series with grouped bars"],[1239,"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values"],[748,"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"single\"` or `\"multiple\"`."],[1627,"**Space / Enter**"],[1082,"**Space**: Select the focused radio button"],[278,"**Space**: Toggles the focused checkbox"],[796,"**Space/Enter**: activate an item; **Escape**: close"],[1207,"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"],[628,"**Sprite Sheet Creation**: A hidden SVG sprite sheet is automatically injected into the DOM containing symbol definitions"],[638,"**SSR Limitation**: Sprite references render empty until client-side hydration"],[1274,"**Standalone** - with no parent context it renders with its own structural defaults and looks the same everywhere."],[883,"**Steppers**: A stepper is a `Group` holding `Button slot=\"decrement\"`, an `Input`, and `Button slot=\"increment\"`. Left empty, each button takes its icon, `variant=\"control\"`, and `size` from the field, so no icon imports are needed. Compose a bare `Input` instead for a plain numeric input"],[1720,"**Sticky axes**: Positioned absolutely to remain visible during scroll"],[1709,"**Sticky y-axis**: The y-axis remains visible during horizontal scroll"],[578,"**Styling**: `className`, `style`, `data-*` attributes"],[622,"**SVG Parsing**: The fetched SVG string is parsed into a React element using `@bento/svg-parser`"],[1623,"**Tab**"],[277,"**Tab**: Moves focus to the next/previous checkbox"],[1079,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the radio group"],[1205,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"],[1530,"**The body is `<Text slot=\"body\">`**, once or as many times as the copy needs."],[1528,"**The eyebrow is `slot=\"eyebrow\"`**, on either a `Text` or a `Tag`. The two forms swap\nfreely, and a `Tag` is sized to pair with the lockup."],[1529,"**The title is `<Heading slot=\"title\">`.** Pick the level from the document outline, not the\nvisual size: `size` handles the visuals, so `level={1}` in an `xs` lockup is perfectly valid."],[1034,"**Titles overflow:** that's expected — titles truncate. Shorten the title."],[1619,"**ToggleButton Item:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1618,"**ToggleButtonGroup Container:** `data-size`"],[1724,"**Tooltips** use absolute positioning and scroll-aware calculations for accurate placement"],[1713,"**Tooltips**: Show on both hover and focus for keyboard users"],[637,"**Trade-offs:**"],[579,"**Transform**: `rotate`, `flip` for icon transformations"],[410,"**Trigger and calendar**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a calendar icon and the formatted value from the field. `DatePickerCalendar` (and `DateRangePickerCalendar`) is the calendar in the popover it opens: it takes `Calendar` props plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `Calendar` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[1237,"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[799,"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"],[1900,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[573,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1692,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1964,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[640,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[641,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[651,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[886,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1241,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1488,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[884,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[1742,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[1684,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[1718,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[1693,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[627,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[1332,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1329,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1338,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1339,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1327,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1333,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1336,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1330,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1342,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[110,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[1943,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1945,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1939,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[1941,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[1946,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[1942,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[1940,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[1944,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[1896,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[524,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1523,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1085,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1210,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[385,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[280,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1086,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1211,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[282,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1088,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1635,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1212,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[384,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[986,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[281,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1087,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[382,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[984,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[983,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value"],[381,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[985,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[383,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[1888,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[109,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[266,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[336,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[354,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[332,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[347,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1564,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[1856,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1020,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[602,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[605,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[601,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[603,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[604,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[606,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1320,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[411,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[444,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[932,"`Enter/Space`"],[486,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[716,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[453,"`Escape`"],[859,"`Escape`"],[934,"`Escape`"],[1569,"`Escape`"],[523,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1925,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[610,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1963,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[663,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[154,"`href` turns the Card into a native link. Modifier-click, middle-click, and \"Open in new tab\" work\non the surface. Body text is not selectable. Do not put CornerActions on an `href` Card. Clicking\nbody text on an `onPress` or selection Card activates it; dragging that text selects it."],[704,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[687,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[155,"`isDisabled` disables only the primary. `isSelectionDisabled` disables only selection. Radio\nread-only and validation state belong on `RadioGroup`."],[1839,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[1894,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[753,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1893,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[788,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[107,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[414,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[854,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[850,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[147,"`onPress` is the Card primary. Nested buttons keep their own hits, so Save does not open the\nModal. Compose a Card inside the Modal when the action is a focused form."],[1019,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1696,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1389,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1559,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[724,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[707,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[926,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[710,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[960,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[965,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child componen